{
  "_comment": [
    "Siwa homepage.",
    "",
    "ORDER SET BY CLIENT, 2026-08-13:",
    "  announcement · header · hero · USP · best selling · collections ·",
    "  bundles · inspired by · layering · UGC videos · reviews · quiz ·",
    "  brief about · footer",
    "",
    "This replaces the earlier DedCool-derived order. Two notes:",
    "  · the quiz now sits LATE (10th of 11) rather than ahead of the",
    "    catalogue. BENCHMARK.md Part 1 §3.5 calls the scent finder the",
    "    biggest missing feature and discovery tools usually convert best",
    "    before the products — but placement is a merchant call, and this",
    "    is it.",
    "  · bundles and layering are separate bands on purpose: bundles sells",
    "    pre-made sets, layering builds a pair. Snif runs both",
    "    (DIRECTION.md Part 1 §2.5); they answer different intents.",
    "",
    "Not in this order, though built and available: stay-close (newsletter",
    "+ WhatsApp referral), recently-viewed, shop-by-mood, logo-list. There",
    "is currently NO email capture anywhere on the homepage — worth a",
    "decision before launch.",
    "",
    "Ground alternates so no two adjacent bands share a colour.",
    "Copy is ported from homepage/js/config.js where it was researched.",
    "",
    "Collection and product references are deliberately EMPTY — they must",
    "be picked against the real store. Inventing handles renders a blank",
    "page that looks broken.",
    "",
    "ONE LANGUAGE AT A TIME (corrected 2026-08-13):",
    "  Parallel `*_ar` fields have been removed from every section and",
    "  snippet. They rendered English and Arabic simultaneously, which is",
    "  not what bilingual means. Arabic content is now supplied through",
    "  Settings → Languages (Translate & Adapt) — Shopify's own translation",
    "  layer — and `request.locale` drives direction, type family, numerals",
    "  and mirroring in layout/theme.liquid.",
    "",
    "  To publish Arabic: add it under Settings → Languages, then translate",
    "  these section settings in Translate & Adapt. Nothing here changes."
